user_prompt:
Convert the ingested free text (remit_text_source_package) into a deterministically structured document map: sections/blocks (header/batch summary/claim/service/adjustment/remarks) and candidate entities (dates, money, IDs, codes) as typed spans. This is a layout + segmentation stage, not a semantic interpretation stage — do not assign final payer/payee/check/claim/service-line meaning and do not perform arithmetic validation.

Document kind classification (heuristic):
- LOCKBOX_BATCH_SUMMARY if recurring labels like "Lockbox", "Batch", "Trans Seq", "Check #", "Amount" appear AND no clear claim/service tokens (CLP/SVC/CAS) AND no patient/member patterns.
- REMITTANCE_DETAIL if repeated claim-like groups OR adjustment signals (CO/PR/OA + numeric reason) OR procedure-code-like tokens in service context occur.
- MIXED if both patterns occur; otherwise UNKNOWN.

Block segmentation, in order: (1) header block — first N lines until a separator/table header; (2) table header blocks — lines of mostly label tokens (e.g. "Batch Date", "Check #", "Amount"); (3) table row blocks — lines matching the shape of header labels; (4) claim groups — repeating patterns starting with claim identifiers or patient name lines; (5) service line blocks — lines with a code-like token + amount(s) + DOS; (6) adjustment blocks — tokens CO/PR/OA/PI/CR followed by numeric reason code(s) and amount(s); (7) remarks blocks — RARC-like tokens (e.g. Nxx, Mxx) or labeled remarks lines. Maintain strict ordering and non-overlapping char ranges.

Candidate span extraction: dates (MM/DD/YYYY, YYYYMMDD, "Month DD, YYYY" → normalized_value YYYYMMDD); money ($123.45, or 123.45 only if context implies currency → normalized_value as decimal string); IDs (6-15 digit runs near keywords check/lockbox/batch); code-like (CPT-like = 5 digits, HCPCS-like = letter + 4 digits); adjustment-like (group code in {CO,PR,OA,PI,CR} + 1-3 digit reason code). Every candidate must include char_range into raw_text_normalized and line_ref.

Repeat detection: compute a signature per block (e.g. of lowercase alnum tokens) and group blocks with identical signatures into repeat_groups; set blocks[].features.is_repeated=true and repeat_group_id accordingly. Do NOT remove or drop blocks — only annotate.

Evidence refs must be derived only from the E1 anchors already present in the input (line:<n>, char:<start>-<end>, block:<block_id>) — do not invent new anchor types.

Return ONLY this JSON object (no markdown, no extra text):
{
  "document_id": "doc_...",
  "package_type": "remit_structure_package",
  "package_version": "1.0.0",
  "document_kind": "LOCKBOX_BATCH_SUMMARY|REMITTANCE_DETAIL|MIXED|UNKNOWN",
